.\" zmakefile(5): the input file of zmake in legacy mode and in modern mode.
.\" Keep in sync with docs/src/content/docs/docs/guides/syntax-modes.md and
.\" guides/tasks-and-phony-inference.md (ADR-0027).
.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt ZMAKEFILE 5
.Os zmake
.Sh NAME
.Nm ZMakefile ,
.Nm Make.zig.mk
.Nd input file of zmake in modern mode and in legacy mode
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr zmake 1
reads each input file in one of two modes.
Both modes use the same expansion, the same pattern rules and the same executor.
.Pp
.Em Legacy mode
keeps strict POSIX and GNU Make semantics.
.Em Modern mode
removes the
.Ic .PHONY
boilerplate and accepts recipe lines that start with spaces.
Modern mode still reads
.Ic .PHONY ,
so a Makefile snippet works in a
.Pa ZMakefile
with no change.
.Ss Mode selection
.Xr zmake 1
applies the first rule that matches:
.Bl -enum
.It
Use
.Fl -modern
or
.Fl -legacy
when the command line gives one.
.It
Otherwise, use the basename of the
.Fl f
file.
.Pa ZMakefile
and
.Pa Make.zig.mk
select modern mode.
Any other name selects legacy mode.
.It
Otherwise, search the directory in this order:
.Pa ZMakefile ,
.Pa Make.zig.mk ,
.Pa GNUmakefile ,
.Pa makefile ,
.Pa Makefile .
.El
.Ss Recipe lines
In legacy mode, a recipe line starts with a tab.
A line with spaces after a rule gives the error
.Ql missing separator .
.Pp
In modern mode, a recipe line starts with a tab, or with two or more spaces.
The first indented line sets the indent of the block.
.Xr zmake 1
removes that indent from each line of the block.
A non-blank line at column 0 ends the block.
Blank lines and comment lines do not end the block.
A recipe line with less indent than the block is an error.
Put variable assignments at column 0.
.Ss Tasks
In modern mode,
.Ic @name:
and
.Ic task name:
declare a task.
A task always runs its recipe.
.Xr zmake 1
never examines the disk for a task.
In a rule with several targets, each target carries
.Ql @ ,
or none does.
In legacy mode,
.Ql @name
and
.Ql task
are ordinary target names.
.Ss Target kinds
In modern mode,
.Xr zmake 1
applies the first rule that matches:
.Bl -enum
.It
A task, or a target that
.Ic .PHONY
names, is a phony target.
.It
A name with
.Ql /
or
.Ql \&. ,
a pattern rule, or a recipe that refers to
.Ql $@
gives a file target.
.It
Any other target with a rule is an inferred phony target.
.El
.Pp
A name with no rule is always a file.
The scan for
.Ql $@
also matches
.Ql $(@) ,
.Ql ${@} ,
.Ql $(@D) ,
.Ql $(@F) ,
.Ql ${@D}
and
.Ql ${@F} .
.Pp
In legacy mode, a target is phony when
.Ic .PHONY
names it.
Any other target is a file.
.Ss Collision warning
An inferred phony target can have the same name as a file or a directory.
.Xr zmake 1
then runs the recipe and prints a warning.
Declare the target as a task, for example
.Ic @test: ,
to remove the warning.
.Ss Partial files
After a failed recipe, legacy mode keeps a partial file target, unless
.Ic .DELETE_ON_ERROR
is a target.
Modern mode deletes the partial file, unless
.Ic .PRECIOUS
names it.
.Ss Directives
Both modes accept
.Ic ifeq ,
.Ic ifneq ,
.Ic ifdef ,
.Ic ifndef ,
.Ic else ,
.Ic endif ,
.Ic define ,
.Ic override ,
.Ic undefine ,
.Ic include ,
.Ic -include ,
.Ic sinclude ,
.Ic export ,
.Ic unexport
and
.Ic vpath .
.Xr zmake 1
stops with an error for a feature that it does not support.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ZMakefile , Pa Make.zig.mk
Input files in modern mode.
.It Pa GNUmakefile , Pa makefile , Pa Makefile
Input files in legacy mode.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A
.Pa ZMakefile
with a task, an inferred phony target and two file targets:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
build:              # inferred phony target
    $(CC) -o app main.c

app: main.c         # the recipe refers to $@: a file
    $(CC) -o $@ main.c

app.tar: app        # the name has a dot: a file
    tar -cf $@ app

@deploy: app.tar    # a task
    ./deploy.sh app.tar
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr zmake 1
.Pp
The guides
.Dq Syntax Modes
and
.Dq Tasks and Phony Inference
at
.Lk https://infrashift.github.io/zmake/
give more examples.
